<title>UK: IPE appoints natural gas specialist.</title>
<headline>IPE appoints natural gas specialist.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Petroleum Exchange (IPE) announced Monday that Stephen Barraclough, a specialist in natural gas markets, joined the exchange.</p>
<p>Barraclough becomes assistant vice president of product development and research, with particular responsibility for natural gas.</p>
<p>He was a consultant on gas transmission and distribution issues, including third party access, tariff design and regulatory regimes before joining the exchange. And before that he was assistant director of network operations at UK industry regulator of gas between 1994 and 1996.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
